          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On Wednesday, June 22 at 11:15 PM, a witness is intrigued by a persistent noise coming from the garden. He looks up at the sky and sees a red point passing through the sky. The point does not flicker and moves quickly. The witness films the object. This testimony is sparse on information, with the questionnaire only partially filled out and the mentioned video not provided, despite reminders from GEIPAN. Given the lack of details, the observation does not seem unusual as it could correspond to several explanations, including a release of a Thai lantern. However, without further information, it is not possible to draw a conclusion. Consequently, GEIPAN classifies it as C: Lack of Information.",
